Control type:
  Velocity-based hybrid control

Main loop rate:
  60 Hz

Camera:
  CAM_INDEX = 0
  CAM_URL = None
  WARP_W x WARP_H = 1280 x 720

Vision processing:
  HSV detection for blue ball
  HSV detection for red bar
  Kalman filter for ball position and velocity
  Predictive intercept control for bar motion

HSV thresholds:
  BLUE_LO = (90, 100, 100)
  BLUE_HI = (100, 255, 255)
  RED1_LO = (0, 120, 70)
  RED1_HI = (10, 255, 255)
  RED2_LO = (170, 120, 70)
  RED2_HI = (180, 255, 255)

Vision-to-robot scaling:
  PIXELS_PER_CM_BAR = 24.0
  M_PER_PX_BAR = 0.01 / 24.0
  CALIB_SIGN = 1

OpenCV direction threshold:
  DIR_THRESHOLD = 0.02 m/s

OpenCV direction mapping:
  vx < -0.02 -> OpenCV direction class 0
  vx > +0.02 -> OpenCV direction class 1
  otherwise  -> None / ambiguous

EEG + Vision fusion:
  EEG always controls direction.
  Vision controls speed magnitude.

EEG direction:
  EEG class 0 -> sign = -1.0
  EEG class 1 -> sign = +1.0

Speed logic:
  If OpenCV direction is available:
    measured speed = abs(opencv_vx)
    speed is clamped to [0.01, V_MAX]

    If EEG class == OpenCV direction:
      speed multiplier = V_FAST_MULT = 1.0
      robot moves fast / full speed

    If EEG class != OpenCV direction:
      speed multiplier = V_SLOW_MULT = 0.5
      robot moves slow / half speed

  If OpenCV direction is not available:
    speed = BASE_VX = 0.177 m/s

Final command:
  vx_cmd = CALIB_SIGN x EEG_direction_sign x speed

No EEG prediction:
  Robot stops.

Held prediction duration:
  VELOCITY_HOLD_S = 0.8 seconds

